# Cloudflare Pages response headers for beakbrain.com.
#
# Added 2026-08-13 after the pre-launch panel review found the site serving only
# x-content-type-options and referrer-policy: no HSTS, no framing protection, no
# Permissions-Policy, and no cache policy of our own.
#
# Rules are additive and every matching block applies, so /* carries the security
# headers for the whole site and the path blocks below add caching on top.
#
# NOTE ON CACHE LIFETIMES: almost nothing on this site has a content-hashed filename,
# so almost no rule here may use `immutable`. A year-long immutable cache on
# /assets/hero.mp4 would pin the old file on every returning visitor's machine with no
# way to bust it short of renaming. The one exception is /birds/assets/site.<hash>.css,
# whose name IS its content, added 2026-08-13 when the Bird Guide stylesheet stopped
# being inlined into every page. The app (beakbrain-app) hashes its filenames
# throughout and uses immutable there too — see birding-app/scripts/pwa-patch.mjs.
#
# CONTENT-SECURITY-POLICY, added 2026-08-21 after measuring what these pages
# actually load rather than guessing. Every script and stylesheet on the site is
# self-hosted — cardmap.js, worldmap.js, maplibre and both site.<hash>.css files —
# so no external script origin is allowed at all.
#
# script-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' and that is the honest limit of this policy: the
# generator writes 15 inline <script> blocks and 14 inline on* handlers across the
# page types, and a hash list cannot cover an on* attribute at all. What the policy
# still buys with it: no script may be FETCHED from another origin, object-src
# 'none' kills plugin embeds, base-uri 'self' stops a <base> tag redirecting every
# relative URL, form-action 'self' stops a form posting off-site, and
# frame-ancestors 'none' backs up X-Frame-Options in browsers that prefer CSP.
# Removing 'unsafe-inline' means moving those handlers into cardmap.js/worldmap.js
# and hashing the remaining blocks in generate.js — worth doing, not worth blocking
# a launch on.
#
# img-src and media-src stay `https:` rather than a host list, for the same reason
# the app's policy does: pictures and audio cannot execute, they are drawn from a
# long tail (upload.wikimedia.org on 383 species pages alone, and growing with the
# taxonomy), and pinning the list would silently blank media on the next data build.
# connect-src is where the tight list belongs, and both entries were found by
# LOADING the pages rather than by reading them: /daily/ posts photo reports to
# Supabase with the publishable key, and the country guides fetch their basemap
# style and tiles from openfreemap. The first draft of this policy omitted
# openfreemap and the guide maps came up as an empty grey canvas with the page
# around them intact — no error, nothing missing above the fold, exactly the kind
# of break that ships. Drive the pages after every change to this line.
#
# worker-src allows blob: because maplibre-gl creates its workers that way; without
# it the world map fails with no visible error, which is the failure mode a CSP is
# most likely to ship unnoticed. Verified by loading the pages and reading the
# console, not by reading this file.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://gvmrwlywoiygjfdqmmem.supabase.co https://tiles.openfreemap.org; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Fonts are self-hosted and effectively never change under the same filename.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# The app screenshots, whose names ARE their content (build/hash-screens.py). Added
# 2026-08-14: replacing the six under fixed names shipped the files and changed
# nothing anybody saw, because the week-long rule below kept serving the old bytes
# from the same URL.
#
# Measured on the live site rather than assumed: Cloudflare Pages MERGES the two
# matching rules instead of letting the more specific one win, so what is actually
# served is `public, max-age=604800, immutable` — this rule contributes `immutable`
# and /assets/* below keeps the week. That is the correct outcome anyway now the
# names are hashed (a week of caching on a URL that can never hold different bytes
# costs nothing), so the year is not worth chasing. Do not read the number here as
# what ships; check the response.
/assets/screens/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Everything else under assets: images, video and the site CSS/JS. A week, so a
# correction still reaches people in reasonable time given these names are not hashed.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# The Bird Guide stylesheet, fetched once for a whole crawl instead of inlined into
# every page. Its filename is a hash of its content, so it can never go stale: editing
# the CSS changes the name. This is the only immutable rule on the site.
/birds/assets/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
